<section class="reading"><p class="eyebrow">THE ENGINEER BEHIND THE NOTES</p><h1>Hello, I’m Sebastian.</h1><p class="lead">A software engineer interested in C++, embedded systems, and the reasoning that connects code to reliable behavior.</p><div class="prose"><h2>Writing to understand</h2><p>This blog is a place to work through engineering questions carefully: what a language feature guarantees, how a design communicates ownership, and why a small implementation detail can change the behavior of a whole system.</p><h2>From rules to real systems</h2><p>The notebook focuses on modern C++, practical embedded software, and software design. Expect small examples, explicit assumptions, and explanations that connect the language rules to everyday engineering decisions.</p><h2>Follow the work</h2><p>You can find the code and follow along on <a href="https://github.com/sebastianmathai">GitHub</a>. For questions or corrections about the blog, visit <a href="https://github.com/sebastianmathai/sebastian-dev-blog">the source repository</a>.</p></div></section>
